	copyright = {Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License},
	url = {http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Moral_panic&oldid=647501100},
	abstract = {A moral panic is an intense feeling expressed in a population about an issue that appears to threaten the social order. Moral panics are in essence controversies that involve arguments and social tension, and in which agreement is difficult because the matter at its centre is taboo. The media are key players in the dissemination of moral indignation, even when they do not appear to be consciously engaged in crusading or muckraking. Simply reporting the facts can be enough to generate concern, anxiety or panic.
